_archive/

# ...but a SUBMISSION archive is a provenance record, not scratch. The rule above
# is unanchored, so it also swallowed `SUBMISSION_2026/TAE/_archive/` -- 165 files,
# 52 MB, of which 88 PNGs and 14 PDFs are rejected figure candidates (correctly not
# versioned) and 25 markdown files are the WRITTEN REASONING for why each was
# refused (which is the part worth keeping). Losing the reasoning and keeping the
# rasters on disk is exactly backwards.
#
# That this was the intent is not a guess: `SUBMISSION_2026/TAE/_archive/**/candidates/*.pdf`
# further down this file is a narrower rule inside an already-excluded directory --
# dead code, written by someone who believed the archive was tracked. It was not.
#
# So: inside a submission workspace's archive, track the records and skip the weight.
# "Archive it" must not silently mean "remove it from version control", or archiving
# a superseded governance document destroys the audit trail it exists to preserve.
# Step 1: let git descend into submission archives at all.
!SUBMISSION_2026/**/_archive/
!SUBMISSION_2026/**/_archive/**/
!ICLR2027/**/_archive/
!ICLR2027/**/_archive/**/
# Step 2: re-exclude everything inside them by default. Negating a directory turns
# OFF the blanket `_archive/` rule for its contents, so without this line the 52 MB
# of rejected rasters would start being versioned -- the opposite of the intent.
SUBMISSION_2026/**/_archive/**
ICLR2027/**/_archive/**
# Step 2b: ...but keep DIRECTORIES traversable. The trailing slash matches directories
# only. Without this, git stops at the first subdirectory and every negation below it
# is dead -- a file inside an excluded directory cannot be re-included, which is the
# most common way a .gitignore silently does the opposite of what it reads like.
!SUBMISSION_2026/**/_archive/**/
!ICLR2027/**/_archive/**/
# Step 3: track only the records. Text, code and config -- the reasoning, never the weight.
# `.tex` and `.patch` are on this list for the same reason as `.md`: a figure's LaTeX
# source and a diff of how a script changed are REASONING, not weight. `.csv` is
# deliberately NOT here -- that is data, and it belongs on the ignored side.
!SUBMISSION_2026/**/_archive/**/*.md
!SUBMISSION_2026/**/_archive/**/*.py
!SUBMISSION_2026/**/_archive/**/*.yml
!SUBMISSION_2026/**/_archive/**/*.yaml
!SUBMISSION_2026/**/_archive/**/*.json
!SUBMISSION_2026/**/_archive/**/*.txt
!SUBMISSION_2026/**/_archive/**/*.tex
!SUBMISSION_2026/**/_archive/**/*.patch
!ICLR2027/**/_archive/**/*.md
!ICLR2027/**/_archive/**/*.py
!ICLR2027/**/_archive/**/*.yml
!ICLR2027/**/_archive/**/*.yaml
!ICLR2027/**/_archive/**/*.json
!ICLR2027/**/_archive/**/*.txt
!ICLR2027/**/_archive/**/*.tex
!ICLR2027/**/_archive/**/*.patch
# Step 4: and never the caches, whatever their extension suggests.
SUBMISSION_2026/**/_archive/**/__pycache__/**
ICLR2027/**/_archive/**/__pycache__/**

